      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Bring a large pot of water to a rolling boil and salt it until it tastes seasoned.",
          "timerMinutes": null,
          "tip": "Under-salted water is the most common reason a finished pasta tastes flat."
        },
        {
          "text": "Warm the olive oil in a wide pan over medium-low heat, add the garlic, and cook until fragrant but not coloured.",
          "timerMinutes": 2,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Add the tomatoes and chilli flakes, raise the heat, and cook until the tomatoes collapse and the sauce thickens.",
          "timerMinutes": 18,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cook the spaghetti one minute short of the package time, reserving a mug of the cooking water before draining.",
          "timerMinutes": 9,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Toss the drained pasta into the sauce with a splash of the reserved water and stir hard until the sauce coats every strand.",
          "timerMinutes": 1,
          "tip": "The starch in the water is what emulsifies the sauce -- plain water will not do it."
        },
        {
          "text": "Kill the heat, fold in the torn basil, taste for salt, and serve with the Parmesan.",
          "timerMinutes": null,
          "tip": null
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Out of season, 2 x 400g tins of good whole plum tomatoes beat fresh ones.",
        "Keeps 3 days refrigerated; loosen with a splash of water when reheating."
      ],
