      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onions until soft and golden.",
          "timerMinutes": 8,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Add the garlic and ginger and cook until fragrant.",
          "timerMinutes": 1,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stir in the curry powder and cook briefly to toast the spices.",
          "timerMinutes": null,
          "tip": "Toasting the spice in the fat before adding liquid wakes up flavour that a wet pan can't."
        },
        {
          "text": "Add the chicken pieces and cook, stirring occasionally, until lightly browned on all sides.",
          "timerMinutes": 6,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Pour in the coconut milk, add salt, and bring to a gentle simmer.",
          "timerMinutes": null,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cover and simmer until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce has thickened slightly.",
          "timerMinutes": 22,
          "tip": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Taste and adjust salt or spice, then garnish with fresh cilantro before serving.",
          "timerMinutes": null,
          "tip": null
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Swap thighs for a firm white fish in the last 8 minutes for a quicker version.",
        "Keeps 3 days refrigerated, and freezes well for up to 2 months."
